  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to my registered residence.
    - Completing the evening census route.
    - Resident returning home before sunset.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Updating the local registry. Some records need correcting.
    - Delivering documentation to the district office.
    - Returning to my apartment. I do not stay out long.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - All remaining residents must be accounted for. I am one of them.
    - The records need to be current. I make sure of that.
    - Going home. The door is always unlocked for me.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Picking up my husband from his shift at the bread factory.
    - New to the district. Looking for the housing office.
    - Paying a fine for filing my own registry form late.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Moving into a shared flat. I cannot bear living alone.
    - Starting at the census office this week. Still in training.
    - Meeting the officer from this post. I have forgotten his name.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Taking my children to the shelter before lockdown.
    - The records no longer matter. I have stopped keeping them.
    - Asking the district office who still lives on my street.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good evening. Here are my documents. Everything is in order, as always.
    - I have all the correct papers. I filed them myself.
    - You are new here. I know the names of everyone who has worked this post.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The registry has some gaps now. That happens in situations like this. I fill them.
    - I keep very careful records. It helps to know who is left.
    - Do not worry. I have been through this checkpoint thirty-one times. I know the procedure.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I counted every checkpoint visit from the beginning. You will want to record that.
    - I always know when something is ending. It is a useful skill.
    - Everything in my file is accurate. I double-check.
