  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d71e962d6af69bf4f8e4449472844fc2, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My evening census route. District eleven, blocks four through nine. Every door answered but two. I noted which two.
    midDaysAnswer: The district office. I delivered corrections to the registry. There are more corrections every week.
    finalDaysAnswer: The last addresses on my list. Most of the doors were open. I recorded what I found inside.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The tram depot. I work the ticket office there. The census forms are only something I help with on Sundays.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The district office. I had to explain why the registry is late. I have been careless with it lately. It happens.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: From the western district. I only moved to this town last month, so I do not know this crossing well.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I keep a record of my own health, as I do for everyone else. There is nothing to enter.
    midDaysAnswer: I sleep less. Three hours, perhaps four. I use the rest of the night to review old entries.
    finalDaysAnswer: Only that I remember things very clearly now. Dates. Faces. It is not always comfortable.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My eyes, a little. Faces blur together these days. I could not tell you who sat at this window before you.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No. I sleep very well. My husband makes sure of it. He does not let me work at night.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Only forgetfulness. I lose names now. Yesterday I could not recall my own block number.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I have recorded every resident in this district. Some of them do not know that.
    - You are the fourth officer to work this post. The third one was quieter.
    - I keep a column for people who look right through me. It is longer than you would think.
    midDays:
    - The list is shorter than it was. That is normal in an emergency. I have read about this.
    - A lot of people are getting very honest lately. It makes my job easier.
    - I wrote your name down. Do not worry. It is only for the registry.
    finalDays:
    - Almost everyone I have recorded in this district is still here. Almost everyone.
    - The numbers do not lie. People do, but numbers do not.
    - I never forget a face. It is not a skill I chose. It just happens.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 7070787
